    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Championships: NBA and WNBA eras\"\n---\n\n\n\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\"}\n## Takeaways\n- **NBA playoffs punish threes and rim attempts.** Points per three-point attempt fell in the playoffs in all\n  23 seasons (−0.040 points per shot). Rim attempts fell in 87% of seasons. Mid-range shots held up best.\n- **WNBA playoffs show no reliable shot-zone penalty.** Every zone's 95% interval includes zero; with 8-12\n  playoff teams a year the sample is small.\n- **The WNBA is about six years behind the NBA on the three-point shift, and the gap has grown.** In 2026,\n  37% of WNBA shots were threes, about where the NBA was in 2019-20. In 2017-2020 the gap was about three years.\n- **Recent WNBA champions are ahead of their own league.** From 2022 to 2026 they took 5 percentage points more of\n  their shots from three, and 7.5 points fewer at the rim, than the league average. NBA champions have stayed within 3 points of their league.\n:::\n\nEverything on this page is association, not causation, and each league is measured against itself.\n\n## Which shots survive the playoffs?\n\nPoints per shot in the playoffs minus the regular season, by zone. Below zero = the shot got worse in the\nplayoffs. Each league is shown on its own.\n\n::: {#9e098a4b .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div>                            <div id=\"5de1b228-764d-4faf-81c7-a211123df305\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:420px; width:100%;\"></div>            <script type=\"text/javascript\">                                    window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                    if (document.getElementById(\"5de1b228-764d-4faf-81c7-a211123df305\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"5de1b228-764d-4faf-81c7-a211123df305\",                        [{\"hovertemplate\":\"NBA three: %{y:+.3f}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",