t_bgcolor\":\"rgba(0,0,0,0)\",\"xaxis\":{\"automargin\":true,\"gridcolor\":\"#e4e3df\",\"linecolor\":\"rgba(0,0,0,0)\",\"zeroline\":false},\"yaxis\":{\"automargin\":true,\"gridcolor\":\"#e4e3df\",\"zeroline\":false}}},\"legend\":{\"y\":1.12},\"height\":340,\"yaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"years behind the NBA\"}},\"xaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"WNBA season\"}}},                        {\"displaylogo\": false, \"responsive\": true}                    )                };                            </script>        </div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## How champions differ from their own league\n\nChampion's share of shots minus its league's share that season, averaged by era (percentage points).\nPositive = the champion took more of that shot than the league did.\n\n::: {#3d2cbfa3 .cell execution_count=5}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**NBA**\n\n| era     |   champions |   threes |   rim |   mid-range |   assisted makes |\n|:--------|------------:|---------:|------:|------------:|-----------------:|\n| 2004-10 |           7 |      1   |   0.9 |        -1.9 |              1   |\n| 2011-16 |           6 |      2.9 |  -1   |        -1.9 |              2.4 |\n| 2017-21 |           5 |      1   |   0.2 |        -1.2 |              3.9 |\n| 2022-26 |           5 |      2.3 |  -0.6 |        -1.7 |              1.4 |\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**WNBA**\n\n| era     |   champions |   threes |   rim |   mid-range |   assisted makes |\n|:--------|------------:|---------:|------:|------------:|-----------------:|\n| 2004-10 |           2 |      3.5 |   0.5 |        -4   |              1.1 |\n| 2011-16 |           6 |     -1.3 |  -0.2 |         1.5 |              3.2 |\n| 2017-21 |           5 |      2.4 |  -0.1 |        -2.3 |              4.2 |\n| 2022-26 |           5 |      5.3 |  -7.5 |         2.2 |             -0.2 |\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Champion identity: offense, defense, and archetype mix\n\nEach champ