\"x0\":0,\"x1\":0,\"xref\":\"x\",\"y0\":0,\"y1\":1,\"yref\":\"y domain\"},{\"line\":{\"color\":\"#8a8984\",\"width\":1},\"type\":\"line\",\"x0\":0,\"x1\":1,\"xref\":\"x2 domain\",\"y0\":0,\"y1\":0,\"yref\":\"y2\"},{\"line\":{\"color\":\"#8a8984\",\"width\":1},\"type\":\"line\",\"x0\":0,\"x1\":0,\"xref\":\"x2\",\"y0\":0,\"y1\":1,\"yref\":\"y2 domain\"}],\"height\":420,\"hovermode\":\"closest\"},                        {\"displaylogo\": false, \"responsive\": true}                    )                };                            </script>        </div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nChampions' archetype minutes share minus the league average, by era (percentage points).\n\n::: {#66294096 .cell execution_count=7}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**NBA**\n\n| era     | identity mix                             |   Connector forward |   Hub big / point forward |   On-ball creator |   Rim-running big |   Secondary guard |   Spot-up 3-and-D wing |\n|:--------|:-----------------------------------------|--------------------:|--------------------------:|------------------:|------------------:|------------------:|-----------------------:|\n| 2004-10 | defense-led 4, balanced 3                |                -2.2 |                       0.2 |               3.4 |              -1.1 |              -4.3 |                    4   |\n| 2011-16 | balanced 5, offense-led 1                |                -6.1 |                      -3.9 |               1.8 |               0.8 |               1.2 |                    6.3 |\n| 2017-21 | balanced 3, offense-led 2                |                -3.4 |                       3.1 |              -2.1 |              -0.6 |              -2.9 |                    6   |\n| 2022-26 | balanced 3, defense-led 1, offense-led 1 |                 2.4 |                      -2.2 |              -1.6 |              -2.2 |               1.5 |                    2.1 |\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**WNBA**\n\n| era     | identity mix                             |   Connector forward |   Hub big / point forward |   On-ball creator |   Rim-running big |   Secondary guard |   Spot-up 3-and-D wing |\n|:--------|:-----------------------------------------|--------------------:|--------------------------:|------------------:|------------------:|------------------:|-----------------------:|\n| 2004-10 | offense-led 1, balanced 1                |                -1.3 |                      -9.3 |              -0.1 |               4.8 |               3.4 |                    2.5 |\n| 2011-16 | offense-led 3, balanced 3                |                 6.9 |                       0   |              -2.3 |              -3.4 |              -1   |                   -0.2 |\n| 2017-21 | balanced 3, offense-led 1, defense-led 1 |                 2.6 |                       0.4 |              -8.2 |              -2.5 |               8.9 |                   -1.3 |\n| 2022-26 | offense-led 2, balanced 2, defense-led 1 |                -4.2 |                      -0.1 |               6.3 |              -9.5 |              -5.7 |                   13.3 |\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Champion ingredients by era\n\nShare of champions with each loosely defined ingredient. They're meant to show drift, not to be a recipe.\n\n::: {#35e9b94e .cell execution_count=8}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**NBA**\n\n| era     |   primary scorer |   secondary scorer |   spacing big |   perimeter defender |   high-usage players |\n|:--------|-----------------:|-------------------:|--------------:|---------------------:|---------------------:|\n| 2004-10 |                1 |               0.86 |          0.57 |                 1    |                 1.71 |\n| 2011-16 |                1 |               1    |          0.5  |                 0.83 |                 1.83 |\n| 2017-21 |                1 |               1    |          0.2  |                 0.8  |                 1.8  |\n| 2022-26 |                1 |               1    |          0.8  |                 0.6  |                 2    |\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**WNBA**\n\n| era     |   primary scorer |   secondary scorer |   spacing big |   perimeter defender |   high-usage players |\n|:--------|-----------------:|-------------------:|--------------:|---------------------:|---------------------:|\n| 2004-10 |             1    |               1    |          1    |                 0.5  |                  1.5 |\n| 2011-16 |             0.33 |               0.83 |          0.67 |                 0.67 |                  1   |\n| 2017-21 |             0.8  |               0.8  |          0.6  |                 0.8  |                  0.6 |\n| 2022-26 |             1    |               1    |          0.8  |                 0.8  |                  1.4 |\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Does roster mix predict titles better than team strength?\n\nForward-chained test: train on past seasons, predict the next champion. Higher log-likelihood is better.\nSo far roster mix does not beat net rating alone in either league.\n\n::: {#8e4b271a .cell execution_count=9}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**NBA**\n\n| model                             |   test seasons |   log-lik (champion) |   log-lik (random pick) |   avg prob. on champion |\n|:----------------------------------|---------------:|---------------------:|------------------------:|------------------------:|\n| net rating only                   |             15 |               -2.058 |                  -2.773 |                   0.152 |\n| net + checklist                   |             15 |               -2.083 |                  -2.773 |                   0.162 |\n| net + roster mix                  |             15 |               -2.271 |                  -2.773 |                   0.14  |\n| net + roster mix + over-use terms |             15 |               -2.285 |                  -2.773 |                   0.143 |\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**WNBA**\n\n| model                             |   test seasons |   log-lik (champion) |   log-lik (random pick) |   avg prob. on champion |\n|:----------------------------------|---------------:|---------------------:|------------------------:|------------------------:|\n| net rating only                   |             10 |               -1.427 |                  -2.079 |                   0.303 |\n| net + checklist                   |             10 |               -1.491 |                  -2.079 |                   0.295 |\n| net + roster mix                  |             10 |               -1.479 |                  -2.079 |                   0.322 |\n| net + roster mix + over-use terms |             10 |               -1.738 |                  -2.079 |                   0.272 |\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Can roster composition alone pick champions?\n\nThe same forward-chained test with **no net rating, win % or team ratings**: only archetype mix, player\nefficiency, stars, age, defensive stats, and which players were available for the playoffs.\n\n::: {#f879351d .cell execution_count=10}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**NBA**\n\n| model                                            |   avg prob. on champion |   champion ranked 1st |   champion in top 3 |\n|:-------------------------------------------------|------------------------:|----------------------:|--------------------:|\n| net rating only (reference)                      |                    0.15 |                  0.33 |                0.6  |\n| archetype mix                                    |                    0.07 |                  0.07 |                0.2  |\n| player quality (efficiency vs role, stars)       |                    0.08 |                  0.13 |                0.27 |\n| mix + quality                                    |                    0.08 |                  0.07 |                0.2  |\n| mix + quality + stats (age, shot diet, defense)  |                    0.1  |                  0.07 |                0.33 |\n| playoff-available roster: mix + quality + stats  |                    0.11 |                  0.2  |                0.47 |\n| two-stage: composition -> predicted net -> title |                    0.09 |                  0.13 |                0.53 |\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n**WNBA**\n\n| model                                            |   avg prob. on champion |   champion ranked 1st |   champion in top 3 |\n|:-------------------------------------------------|------------------------:|----------------------:|--------------------:|\n| net rating only (reference)                      |                    0.3  |                   0.7 |                 0.8 |\n| archetype mix                                    |                    0.16 |                   0.3 |                 0.5 |\n| player quality (efficiency vs role, stars)       |                    0.21 |                   0.3 |                 0.8 |\n| mix + quality                                    |                    0.18 |                   0.2 |                 0.4 |\n| mix + quality + stats (age, shot diet, defense)  |                    0.2  |                   0.2 |                 0.7 |\n| playoff-available roster: mix + quality + stats  |                    0.25 |                   0.3 |                 0.8 |\n| two-stage: composition -> predicted net -> title |                    0.16 |                   0.2 |                 0.5 |\n:::\n:::\n\n\nRoster-only models beat a random pick but not net rating yet. The strongest one counts only players available\nfor the playoffs.\n\n::: {.caveat}\n*In progress:* lineup eras (small ball, double bigs), playoff-available rosters, team defensive profiles,\nand roster age and size.\n:::\n\n",
